  description:
  - 'An increase in metabolism has evolved the local species of hares to become hyperactive.
    Common observed behaviors include mass production of underground passage ways
    and an insatiable appetite, as well as increased fecundancy. '
  - It is estimated that the local hare population will double every 2 years, classifying
    this species as invasive.
  leftText: 
  rightText: Krakhens run aimlessly, hoping to forage any nearby plants they happen
    to come across. Born through a genetic mutation of Firecracker Hen eggs left
    in the mist, they lack any form of vision. However, they have remarkable tracking
    skills once a potential threat has been identified. Collectively, the large tendrils
    serve as both a brain and a tongue.
